---
// Figma node 14196:20373 ("Mask group"): the hand-held iPhone photo cropped to a
// 1055.34x964 frame whose alpha mask fades the image out toward the bottom
// (linear gradient, opaque until ~81.5%, transparent by ~97%).
//
// This photo is by far the heaviest thing on the page and it straddles the fold,
// so the preload scanner would otherwise start it at the same priority as the
// hero backdrop above it. `fetchpriority="low"` keeps it eager — it is still
// requested on first pass, nothing pops in — but lets the LCP backdrop, the CSS
// and the fonts have the connection first.
---

<section class="relative z-10 mx-auto mt-[5px] w-full max-w-[1055px]">
  <div class="phone-mask relative w-full overflow-clip" style="aspect-ratio: 1055.34 / 964;">
    <img
      src="/images/hero-phone-mockup.png"
      alt="A hand holding an iPhone showing the Fibu lesson screen with planet-themed coding lessons"
      class="absolute max-w-none"
      style="left: -8.82%; top: 4.84%; width: 121.58%; height: 90.21%;"
      width="4096"
      height="2731"
      decoding="async"
      fetchpriority="low"
    />
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .phone-mask {
    -webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, #000 81.5%, transparent 97%);
    mask-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, #000 81.5%, transparent 97%);
  }
</style>
